<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Parser edge cases. Opened by -Dblockui.testgui=parser.

    Every pane here is a probe of com.ldtteam.blockui.Parsers / PaneParams rather than of a widget. The rule for
    this file is that BlockUI must *shrug*: an attribute it cannot make sense of falls back to the default, an
    unknown attribute is ignored, a texture that is not there renders as missingno. Nothing in here may throw,
    and each probe says on screen what it expects, so a mismatch is visible without reading the source.

    The loudest thing this file found: a SIX-digit "#RRGGBB" colour parses to alpha 0x00 and therefore draws
    nothing at all. Parsers.COLOR runs Integer.parseInt(hex, 16) over whatever the pattern matched and never fills
    the alpha byte in, so "#FF3333" is 0x00FF3333 - fully transparent - while "#FFFF3333" is the visible one. Both
    are on screen below, one line apart, and that pair is the point of the section. Nothing in this mod's own
    layouts uses the six-digit form any more; a consuming mod that does has invisible text and no error to explain
    it. Left as a finding rather than fixed here, because making six digits opaque would change how every existing
    layout in every consuming mod renders.

    Two cases are deliberately NOT here because they do throw, and shipping a layout that crashes would defeat
    the point. Both are written up in the report that came with this file:
      - a size/pos whose value matches no number at all (size="wide") — Parsers.SCALED returns null and Pane's
        constructor unboxes it into a NullPointerException;
      - an <image> whose source= is absent or not a parseable Identifier — Image's constructor requires it and
        SafeError.throwInDev rethrows in a dev workspace.

    This is the ONE layout in the mod that deliberately does not validate against block_ui.xsd, because four of
    its probes are about the parser being laxer than the schema. xmllint (with the "schema" option pointed at block_ui.xsd)
    must report exactly these and nothing else:

        enabled="disabled"                      not an xs:boolean, but Parsers.BOOLEAN reads it as false
        enabled="TRUE"                          not an xs:boolean either, but Boolean.parseBoolean accepts it
        nosuchattribute= / anotherone=          unknown attributes, which every pane ignores
        textalign="NOWHERE"                     unknown enum constant, which Parsers.ENUM logs and defaults

    A fifth failure appearing here means either the schema or the parser moved; both are worth a look.
-->
